  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_ad404d87f5e94a1795fdfa2954262141",
      "statement": "The HTTP surface is a deliberately thin transport layer: http_api.py routes requests, parses JSON bodies and caps their size, applies per-IP rate limits, serializes the stable error envelope, and signs audit responses; validation, orchestration, and state changes live in DirectoryService and its sub-services, and every state change is persisted and appended to the L5 audit chain in one Store transaction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/http_api.py#L1-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5964913db9af69fe06eb685ee8bd0bcfbcb36497e6eb98b4b7ec2ac3e80d5d3a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/service.py#L1-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6fe092e6443025a999807efbfbd965848cbb027575137dd2498485a6f7ff8018:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5d9b80103d2e4b8ea25b05bd79b06dee",
      "statement": "DirectoryHTTPServer.build constructs the SQLite Store, the DirectoryService, and the RateLimiterSet; start() and serve_forever() bind a stdlib ThreadingHTTPServer with daemon_threads on config.host:port (default 0.0.0.0:8444), launch a background thread that signs audit checkpoints on the checkpoint_interval_s cadence, and stop() shuts down the socket, signs one final checkpoint on shutdown, then closes the store.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/config.py#L24-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c33e1672d1135b8d64dc00ec4e817b8bf65e7fbd568c053d2ff29fec973756d9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/http_api.py#L78-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:41de0a3f3a37627fc7abba8bfb7c658e7394f9e4b5ae69d1d9e765a162e8ec96:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c400833754fb45bda343e274773b66a1",
      "statement": "Each request runs on a handler that dispatches do_GET, do_POST, and do_DELETE through an ordered route table of literal path comparisons then anchored regexes; a path matching no branch falls through to a 404 NOT_FOUND envelope, DirectoryError raised anywhere in a handler is converted to its error envelope, and any other exception is converted to INTERNAL_ERROR (500) so internals never reach the wire.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/http_api.py#L227-L302",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:abd47fb962df676f13f7afa74a7d2cc7d15a8fdcce323ad28bf975177932a0a4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/http_api.py#L375-L481",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:04885e8fb02afa9f895bd531d895228acf91aca4b6db86007ec24c4b03f68304:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_80d86085868c40e18aadfd5f499db291",
      "statement": "Agent routes are anchored to the fingerprint pattern HF-[0-9a-f]{16}: one regex accepts both /v1/agents/{fp} and the legacy /agents/{fp} prefix and the difference is purely serialization (full {manifest, trust} object vs bare manifest), while per-agent sub-resources (vouches, reports, audit, suspend, unsuspend, appeal) and the vouches/reports/takedown verbs are v1-only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/http_api.py#L295-L297",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ec35bfd7d5274c6819f19223b82e890ee6c9333ed97a5583fe50719e0d9717b:"
