    {
      "id": "claim_1a5482c26bca4a74844fa0f1175bba66",
      "statement": "Rate limiting is per-client-IP, in-memory token buckets (continuous refill, injectable clock, per-instance scope): RateLimiterSet exposes search (rate_search_per_min, default 60 per 60 s) applied to GET /v1/search and /search, and register (rate_register_per_hour, default 5 per 3600 s) applied to POST /v1/register, /register, /v1/verify-domain, and /v1/verify-domain/confirm. Denial returns 429 RATE_LIMITED with a Retry-After header computed as whole seconds until a token is available; business-cap 429s such as VOUCH_LIMIT_REACHED and VERIFICATION_LIMIT_REACHED go out without Retry-After because only the token-bucket path sets retry_after.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/config.py#L37-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:504d6d918707cbed85d13d24133e45e2d9f67eb3177e040cec3c5998cf7fdf9b:"
