    {
      "id": "claim_53c6252242ce4067a09a95ce43892a6d",
      "statement": "The rate-limit key is _client_ip(): by default (trust_proxy_headers false) the TCP peer address is always used and spoofed forwarding headers cannot change a bucket; when trust_proxy_headers is enabled the first element of CF-Connecting-IP or X-Forwarded-For (checked in that order) is used only when the TCP peer is loopback (127.0.0.1 or ::1), otherwise the peer is used because the headers are spoofable.",
